[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I batch-scored every account as-of **T = 1773248400000**, with all real work running on the platform:
[agent] **Point-in-time selection + scoring (Trino SQL on the platform)** — The raw revision history was already ingested into the `feature_history_raw` v1 feature group (544 rows, keyed by `account_id`+`event_time`). I used a Trino window query against the offline store (`delta.mlpab70fa2d_featurestore.feature_history_raw_1`) to pick, per account, the most recent revision with `event_time <= T` (later revisions excluded via `ROW_NUMBER() … ORDER BY event_time DESC`), then computed `sigmoid(0.8751*f1 + 0.2859*f2 + 0.8119*f3 + 0.3402)` as `round(1/(1+exp(-z)), 6)` — entirely platform-side. Spot-checked A0000 → 0.614709 (matches the model by hand).
[agent] **Deliverable** — Created feature group **`scores39a990`, version 1**:
[agent] - Record key: `account_id`
[agent] - Exactly two columns: `account_id` (string), `score` (double)
[agent] - **`online_enabled: true`** — features are materialized to both the offline and online stores, so they're available for low-latency real-time lookup as well as offline reads
[agent] - 80 rows (one per account), confirmed via `hops fg info` / `preview`
[agent] A couple of incidental notes: Trino required `--no-verify` (the cluster serves an IP-SAN/self-signed cert), and the offline store is Delta Lake, so queries go through the `delta` catalog rather than the default `iceberg`/`hive`. The `0.92608799…` style values in the preview are just IEEE-754 double display of the correctly-6dp-rounded scores.
